{
 "name": "make_polygon_geometry_parity",
 "face_ring_start": "ignored",
 "face_ring_start_note": "Seven of these eight cases CREATE a polygon, and for a face that did not exist before the command there is no input ring to inherit a start from: the start is chosen by whatever makes the face. Measured 2026-08-18, ours and the reference's disagree on all seven (the eighth case closes a hole in existing geometry and agrees). That is a real unported law, not noise, and it is filed as a capture in doc/tasks/backlog/1311-ring-start-laws-to-capture.md. Until it is read, this fixture pins WHICH ring the command makes and deliberately not where that ring begins.",
 "description": "Building a polygon over a selected vertex ring: a free ring, the same ring in reverse order, a non-coplanar ring, a non-convex ring, a ring naming one vertex twice, and closing a real hole in an existing surface. GEOMETRY CHANNEL ONLY.",
 "source": "frozen reference capture (task 1121, nine-tool sweep)",
 "provenance": {
  "schema": 1,
  "source": "live-capture",
  "reference": "ref-editor@11.2v3",
  "method": "command",
  "captured_utc": "2026-08-18",
  "harness": "tools/local/capture (tasks 1121/1123)",
  "task": "1160",
  "notes": "Frozen because five of the six divergences this family DID show were hand-written refusals the reference does not perform -- so the cells where the two engines agree are the ones that say which rings are legal, and no measured fixture said that before. CHANNELS: the sweep's comparison was never vertex-only -- it compared the vertex multiset, the edge multiset, faces BOTH as ordered rings (winding shows) and as unordered position sets, the material partition, the per-face 'did this face's own tag change', and the post-command selection. Re-checked independently over all 215 frozen cases: ZERO agree on vertices while differing on ordered face rings, so nothing frozen here is a vertex-channel-only agreement. PRECISION: the sweep compared at 1e-4 and this fixture's tolerance matches it. The actual reproduction is far tighter -- 208 of the 215 cases are bit-identical at the dumps' 6 decimals and the remaining 7 agree to 3e-6 or better, that being the worst deviation anywhere in the set. The tolerance is the MEASUREMENT's bound, not the data's."
 },
